BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8bf5f61e-a7e1-41e6-aede-7b87e4beebab@spacex-launch-alerts
DTSTAMP:20261125T182204Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261125T182204Z
SEQUENCE:217794124
SUMMARY:🚀 Falcon 9 · CHORUS
DTSTART:20261204T125500Z
DTEND:20261204T132400Z
LOCATION:Space Launch Complex 40\, Cape Canaveral SFS\, FL\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: Go for Launch\nWindow: Fri\, 04 Dec 2026 12:55:00 UTC 
 – Fri\, 04 Dec 2026 13:24:00 UTC\nOrbit: Low Earth Orbit\nPad: Space Lau
 nch Complex 40\, Cape Canaveral SFS\, FL\, USA\n\n▶ Watch live: https://
 x.com/i/broadcasts/2VNlrbYvYNmMgM\n\nCHORUS is MDA's next generation Earth
  observation constellation\, consisting of 2 radar satellites (C-band SAR 
 and X-band SAR)\, in a 53.5 degree 600 km altitude LEO\, with the X-band t
 railing the C-band by 60 minutes. A collaborative multi-sensor constellati
 on\, CHORUS will bring together diverse and unique imagery and data source
 s and provide a new level of near real-time insight and innovative Earth o
 bservation services. Operating in a unique mid-inclination orbit\, CHORUS 
 will be able to image day or night\, regardless of weather conditions\, wi
 th daily access of up to 95% of the coverage area. From an industry-leadin
 g 700km-wide imaging swath down to sub-metre high resolution\, CHORUS will
  provide the most extensive and unrivalled Earth observation radar imaging
  capacity available on the market in a single mission.\n\nAlso on board th
 is mission are 2 satellites from ICEYE and PECCY.\n\nCountdown & updates: 
 https://benjaminowens612.github.io/spacex-launch-alerts/#8bf5f61e-a7e1-41e
 6-aede-7b87e4beebab
URL:https://x.com/i/broadcasts/2VNlrbYvYNmMgM
CATEGORIES:other
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
